WEBVTT

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.690
Is that...?!

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.900
If I recall, his name is
William James Moriarty.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.110
Second son of the Moriarty family,
the young mathematics prodigy.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:39.280
I see. So that is the man
with whom I am competing.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:45.620
Then I must thoroughly investigate him
at once, and add him to the list.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.130
Yes, the list...

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:52.420
...kept by me, Charles Augustus Milverton.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.070
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.820
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.950
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.000
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.420
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.800
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.180
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.760
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.350
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.480
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.110
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.240
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.330
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:05.660
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.120
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.000
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.800
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.680
"The Merchant of London"

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.430
"The Merchant of London"
Okay, this time...

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.940
...there is a certain number
that goes into these boxes.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.150
Do you know what it is?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.150
Huh?

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:40.360
Twelve of one thing and twenty of
the other can't be the same number.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.950
Maybe this problem was a bit too hard.
The correct answer is...

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:48.870
Huh? How can it be one?

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.210
These are units of money.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.050
Twelve pence is one shilling.
Twenty shillings is one pound.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:01.180
Which means that one pound is 240 pence.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:06.390
Let me see... If it were bread,
that would buy roughly 240 loaves.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.020
240 loaves?!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.100
Amazing!

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.850
So, if it were 100 pounds...

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.400
Let's see...

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.360
--24,000 loaves!
--24,000 loaves!

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.280
That's more than I could eat
in my whole life!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.910
This is all we get again?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.840
Here, you can eat mine. I'm full already.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.380
Thank you.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.550
Madam...

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.970
You two...

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:51.810
What brings you here
so late in the evening?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.110
We thought that there must be
something troubling you.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:58.980
That perhaps someone had swindled
the orphanage out of its money.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.740
Am I wrong?

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.410
How did you know that?

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:08.870
You are aware that the orphanage
and the almshouse

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:13.870
are supported by the donations
of those in the nobility, yes?

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:19.090
Last month, an aristocrat named
Lord Baxter came here...

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:26.510
Please, I only require another 300 pounds
to construct the orphanage.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:30.470
I'm led to believe that you received
a generous donation the other day.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:36.440
I ask, not for my sake, but for the
orphans, if I could borrow that money?

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.070
I finally found the perfect plot
on which to build the orphanage,

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.990
but if I do not put a deposit
down on it at once,

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.860
they say it will be sold to someone else.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.910
B-But...

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.540
If, by any chance, something happens
to prevent me from returning the money,

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.790
then I will offer myself in exchange.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.290
They were not my own personal funds,

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:01.000
so I knew upfront that it would be
wrong for me to lend it out,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.380
but he had given me a
certificate of borrowing,

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.550
and I thought that since he was
a nobleman, it would be all right...

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.100
...so I...

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.350
However, even after the appointed day
had passed, there was no indication

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.390
that he would pay the money back,

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:17.400
nor was there any sign of
construction for the orphanage.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.820
Would you mind...
if I had a look at this certificate?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.870
Mm...

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.800
You there, is something the matter?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.140
Here, go get yourselves something to eat.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.640
We do not need your alms, Mr Baxter.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.890
We are here on behalf of the
madam from the orphanage.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:59.690
I trust you know of whom I speak.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:06.700
Is the madam feeling under
the weather, perhaps?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.490
Her hands are full tending
to the orphanage.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.530
I see.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:16.290
I expect this concerns the
300 pounds that I borrowed.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:20.290
Unfortunately, construction of
the orphanage has not proceeded,

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.880
and I am having difficulty finding
someone to manage everything.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.010
There is too much for me to handle.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.260
Mr Baxter.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:32.470
We are not here to ask about the progress
of the orphanage construction,

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:37.140
but are here rather to ask you to
return the money that you borrowed.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:42.560
I beg your pardon. Next month, I will be
earning some money through my trading,

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.900
and once that happens, I intend
to repay the money immediately.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.030
I appreciate you saying so,

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.660
but the truth is, we do not even
have enough to eat right now.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:58.160
If you do not repay the money at once,
our orphanage will be unable to operate.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:01.420
I am well aware of the
importance of that money.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.920
However, I cannot return
what I do not have.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.380
Very well. In that case,

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:14.850
what if I were to assume the 300-pound
debt you incurred with the madam?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:23.610
There is 300 pounds here.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.360
How does a child like you
have this much money?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.530
I have been consulting with many adults

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.990
and saving up what they have
rewarded me, little by little.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:38.370
And, out of consideration for the
circumstances you just told us about...

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:45.630
...I will personally lend you
an additional 300 pounds.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:49.010
Will this not be enough to get
construction started without delay?

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:54.390
So you're saying that my debt to
the orphanage will be written off

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:58.020
and I will be borrowing
600 pounds from you?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.690
Thank you! I would like to take you up
on your offer, by all means!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:06.520
Will the same conditions as the contract
I had with the madam suffice?

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:11.450
Yes. I will accept the same
conditions, to the letter.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:14.490
Your repayment date will be
the first day of next month.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.620
All right, that settles it.
Let's take this to the notary right away!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.170
Here is the remaining 300 pounds
we are lending you,

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:28.880
after taking out the amount that
you borrowed from the madam.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:33.050
I am sure that I can repay you
by the first of next month.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.390
Very well.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:39.350
We will go and deliver the 300
pounds to the madam, then.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:58.490
I now once again have enough money
to amuse myself as freely as I like.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:04.790
This world is made so those who
are uncultured lose everything.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.710
If you must curse something, curse the
situation in which you find yourselves!

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:17.510
Brother, are you sure about lending
that man another 300 pounds?

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:22.640
Yes. I lent it under the same
conditions as the madam.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:25.270
Read the last provision.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:32.150
"If the borrower is unable to pay back
the debt by the specified date,

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:35.570
the lender is permitted to
cut out one pound of flesh

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:38.990
from wherever he would like
on the borrower's body."

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.790
Brother, do you mean to
tell me this contract is...?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.910
Yes.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:50.420
The same agreement that the usurer
Shylock and the merchant Antonio

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:57.300
entered into in William Shakespeare's
<i>The Merchant of Venice</i>.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:02.560
In the play, the court does not
allow Shylock to cut out his flesh,

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.190
nor does he even get the money
he lent returned to him.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.440
Oh, that will not happen to us, Louis.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.360
We're going to turn things around.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.820
In the most famous court
case in all the world.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.840
We will now begin the inquiry
into the default

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.590
of the loan agreement entered into
by both the plaintiff and the defendant.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:42.930
This trial will be on the record,
in accordance with statute.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.680
False testimony is a punishable
offence in this court,

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.810
so make sure to choose
your words with care.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.770
Are both parties ready?

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:56.190
I couldn't believe my eyes
when I read the complaint,

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:00.320
but surprisingly enough,
he is just a child.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:04.490
All right, we will begin with an opening
statement from the plaintiff.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.160
Yes, My Lord.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.460
As it states in my complaint,
I, the plaintiff,

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:13.210
seek immediate repayment of
the 600 pounds designated

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:17.170
in the bond agreed to by
the defendant, Mr Baxter.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:21.590
Very well. Now, the defendant
may make his statement.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:26.470
The defendant, Lord Baxter,
has zero current assets,

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:30.390
as documented in the materials
heretofore submitted.

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.940
It must be said that the sum
cannot be immediately repaid,

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:36.980
as demanded by the plaintiff.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.860
Excuse me, My Lord,
but concerning that statement,

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:43.700
I have doubts as to the
defendant's financial position.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.450
Permission to question him?

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.540
Granted.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:52.420
According to these documents,
you currently have no asset holdings,

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:58.260
but, Mr Baxter, you currently reside
in a high-class residential area.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:02.220
Has it not occurred to you
to sell your residence?

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:06.430
Unfortunately, I cannot do that.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:08.140
Why would that be?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:14.770
I am borrowing that estate from
a friend; it is not my property.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:17.820
I see. Moving on, then.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:21.490
You operate a trading company, yes?

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.820
If you were to sell off the ship
owned by the company,

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:28.910
or even the company itself, would it not
be possible to make repayment?

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:31.500
I cannot do that, either.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:36.790
Whilst the trading company does
exist on paper, it has no buildings,

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.010
and the trader on which I had pinned
my hopes became shipwrecked

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.970
and is not returning to port.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.470
The insurance has already been
set aside for the company's losses,

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:49.640
but practically speaking,
it is in bankruptcy.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.150
So as with your estate, you do not
count it amongst your assets,

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:58.110
which is why it is not included
in your documentation?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.360
That is correct.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:04.860
It truly is a pathetic tale,
but whilst I may still have my title,

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:09.790
I have no possessions to my name.
I am a fallen aristocrat!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:18.090
Indeed. It appears that
repayment is impossible.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:19.710
What would you like to do?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:28.350
It would seem that I have no choice...
but to give up on being repaid.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:31.390
As such...

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:36.850
...I request, in accordance with the
other provision in the contract...

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:41.610
...to extract one pound of flesh
from the body of the defendant.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:47.870
Are you seriously requesting
a pound of flesh?!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:55.250
Of course. We had this contract
officially issued by a notary solicitor.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.790
If this is not recognised,

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:01.500
then the entire nation's sovereignty
must be called into question.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:06.130
It is true that contractually,
the request must be recognised...

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.860
J-Just a moment!

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:28.240
My Lord, we recognise that a pound
of flesh may be cut out...

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:33.200
However, the stipulation in the contract
is only for "one pound of flesh."

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.250
In other words, when cutting
out that one pound of flesh,

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:41.080
the shedding of a single drop of blood
is unacceptable! Am I correct?!

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.300
Sustained.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:51.050
Contractually, the plaintiff may not
shed the blood of the defendant.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:59.140
One drop... Cutting out his flesh without
spilling a single drop of blood...

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.230
...is impossible.

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.730
I've won!

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:11.160
Foolish urchin! The moment you signed
this contract, my victory was assured!

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:15.790
I also obtained your assurance that you
would politely forfeit that 600 pounds.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.420
Not a single one of your
demands will be met now!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.040
Then...

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:27.380
...please allow me to continue
to question the defendant.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.050
May the plaintiff be permitted to call
a witness into the courtroom?

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.650
Who is this bloke? It seems like I've...

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.400
If I may first direct my
question to the defendant...

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:51.150
Mr Baxter, you enjoy ordering steak
at restaurants, do you not?

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.740
Yes, from time to time.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.950
Then if I may stand in as the waiter,

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.250
please place your order
as you normally would.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:04.920
Hmm? "Grill me a half-pound
of beef." Will that do?

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.590
Thank you very much.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:09.550
Now, I will question the
witness, Mr Bremner.

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.840
Oh, right.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:16.640
You are a waiter at the restaurant that
Mr Baxter frequents, are you not?

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.220
I am.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:20.520
Ah, that's right.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.940
Do you wait on Mr Baxter often?

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:26.730
Yes. He came in just yesterday.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:30.240
On that occasion, did he have a steak?

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:34.070
Is this urchin trying to insinuate
that because I order steak often,

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:37.580
that I must actually have
money, or something?

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:42.160
Yes. He seemed to relish it
as he always does.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:46.420
So Mr Baxter always orders
his favourite cut of steak

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.800
and is able to pay for it, correct?

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.930
Well, yes, that is correct.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:58.180
Well then, when Mr Baxter orders,

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:04.230
has he ever asked you to remove the
weight of the blood from the meat?

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.730
Ah!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:10.860
The weight of the blood?
No, I have done this for 20 years,

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:14.320
but never once has anyone ever asked that.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.620
I trust my point has been made.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:19.330
N-No! This is, er...

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:23.870
This, in short, concerns
the concept of "flesh."

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:27.840
Earlier, you said that when
cutting out a pound of flesh,

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:32.920
not a single drop of blood
could be permitted to be spilt.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:38.430
However, when Mr Baxter is a customer
placing his regular order,

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:45.060
it is evident that his concept of meat
includes the blood contained within it.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.060
No, you're wrong--

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:49.400
If I am wrong, then you
would have asked

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:54.360
to remove the weight of the
blood whenever you ordered.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:58.320
However, not once did you do so.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:02.490
Meaning that it has been
conclusively demonstrated

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:05.160
that when you signed your name
to the contract, in your mind,

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.460
a pound of flesh included the
weight of the blood within it.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:11.000
Th-That's... chicanery!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.760
I believe <i>you're </i>the one
doing the chicaning.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:20.680
Your own barrister said that he recognised
that a pound of flesh may be cut out.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.350
My Lord?

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.220
He is correct.

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.640
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:30.360
You don't even know the play
on which your contract is based!

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:36.700
"O, Antonio...

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:40.740
If thou art prepared to accept
Shylock's knife into thy bosom,

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:44.240
then lay bare thy breast!"

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:50.080
I can recite from memory the lines
from all of Shakespeare's 40 works.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:55.170
I-Impossible! How can this
poor street urchin...?

00:18:56.300 --> 00:19:00.340
Very well, now that the matter
of blood has been settled...

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:06.890
...it is time at last for me to
exact my pound of flesh.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:09.480
We do not need to allow
the others to watch this.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.360
Wait, you...

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.190
No, really...

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.110
N-No...

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:25.290
Wait... Wait... Please wait!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:28.500
It's all a lie!

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:33.500
I only transferred the title to my home
and my company to a friend.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.710
The truth is, I actually own all of it!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:48.480
H-Half! I'll give you half of all my
property! Just please spare me!

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.980
Half?

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:58.360
All of it. All of your
worldly possessions.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.820
Then we will have a deal.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.830
A-Agreed...

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:14.670
Following the trial, the young men

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:17.750
donated the vast wealth they obtained
from Baxter to the orphanage,

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.720
and then disappeared.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:24.680
Upon investigating the adopted
third son who perished in that fire,

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.890
I arrived at this court record.

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:32.560
There is no doubt about it.
He is the current middle Moriarty boy,

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:35.400
William James Moriarty.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:42.740
After the family manor had burnt down,
he took the place of the real William.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:46.240
And judging by the fact that
the other brothers accept him,

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:50.040
one can presume that all
of the brothers are complicit.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:56.630
William James Moriarty... is...

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.920
...my enemy.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:07.760
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:15.980
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:26.570
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:29.950
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:33.960
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:37.330
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:44.760
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:53.350
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:21:55.350 --> 00:22:01.150
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:07.410
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:10.200
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:15.870
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:22.550
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:34.020
I bring news.

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:38.730
Someone has taken away that court
record that you left to be found.

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.110
The man who took it is
Charles Augustus Milverton.

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:46.820
It appears that his objective
was not to find precedent,

00:22:46.820 --> 00:22:50.240
but to investigate William's past.

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:55.700
Lord Milverton... A man who owns many
newspapers and advertising firms,

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:58.540
who has been nicknamed the King of Media.

00:22:58.540 --> 00:23:02.790
Though not a nobleman, he is nonetheless
a prominent businessman.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:05.210
What is Will's court record?

00:23:05.210 --> 00:23:10.340
Back when William was a kid,
he went up against a nobleman in court.

00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:13.060
Why would you leave
such a thing to be found?

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:15.720
You don't mean--!

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:18.020
Everyone listen here.

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:22.650
It is clear that he is targeting me.

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:25.820
You should all be wary of this man.

00:23:27.110 --> 00:23:31.870
Henceforth, you are to consider
him our most significant foe...

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:35.790
...and eliminate him.

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:50.630
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The White Knight of London Act 1."
